course: dictionary
lesson: 14339
title: Words about work
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller words you may know. Occupational comes from occupation, which is another word for a job, and the ending -al means to do with. So occupational means to do with a job or work. Read the words around it to check your idea.
explain: «Falling off a ladder can be an occupational hazard for builders.» Builders climb ladders as part of their job, so a danger that comes with the job fits here. Ask: what word would fit? A danger that comes with work fits, so occupational means to do with work.
explain: «The nurse said the occupational therapist would help Sam learn to dress himself again after his arm was hurt.» Sam needs help with everyday tasks, and an occupational therapist is the person who gives that help. The clues show that the word is about helping people with daily life.
explain: You will see occupational words in health, safety and careers. When the clues are not enough, a dictionary or a grown-up can help you check.
fact: Occupational means to do with a person's job or work.
fact: Occupational can also mean caused by or happening because of someone's work, as in «occupational injury».
fact: An «occupational hazard» is a danger that comes with a particular job.
fact: An «occupational therapist» helps people with everyday tasks after illness or injury, and helps children who need support with skills like writing or dressing.
fact: «Occupational health» is about keeping people well and safe at work.
exercise: «Lifting heavy boxes is an occupational hazard for movers.» What is an occupational hazard? | A holiday for workers | A fun game played at work | *A danger that comes with a job | A kind of ladder
exercise: Mum is going to her occupational health appointment at work. What does occupational mean here? | To do with school holidays | To do with food | *To do with work | To do with the weather
exercise: «The occupational therapist came to school to help Mia with her writing.» Find and copy the word that means to do with a job. | school | *occupational | therapist | writing
test: What does «occupational injury» mean? | An injury that happens to a cat | An injury from a fall at the park | An injury that never hurts | *An injury caused by someone's work
test: What does «occupational therapy» help with? | Playing football at the weekend | Growing vegetables in a garden | *Everyday tasks after illness or injury | Building new roads
exam: «The builder wore a helmet because falling bricks are an occupational hazard on site.» What does occupational hazard mean? | A type of weather | A game for children | *A danger that comes with the job | A tasty snack
